thout prescription</article-title><source>Hum Reprod</source><year>2004</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>553</fpage><lpage>557</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14998950</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/humrep/deh128</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marston</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Meltzer</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Majeed</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Impact on contraceptive practice of making emergency hormonal contraception available over the counter in Great Britain: repeated cross sectional surveys</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2005</year><volume>331</volume><fpage>271</fpage><lpage>273</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16009669</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.38519.440266.8F</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bacon</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Savage</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Training and supporting pharmacists to supply progestogen-only emergency contraception</article-title><source>J Fam Plann Reprod Health Care</source><year>2003</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>17</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12681032</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1783/147118903101197476</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Office for National Statistics</collab></person-group><source>Contraception and Sexual Health, 2003</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>Office for National Statistics, London</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink